## Slide 6

Installation Manager: Overview

Overview
Primary tool used to manage the installation of TrakSYS™ services and components.
Manage, troubleshoot and maintain an implementation after the initial deployment.
Main Screen 
Acts as a status overview of the various elements of the installation
Provides a menu to interact with details and options in each section.
Has various installation-wide settings for capabilities like Auditing, Notifications, and Web settings.

## Slide 7

Installation Manager: Database

Database Connection Overview
Displays the current status of the application connection to the TrakSYS database. Including login information, SQL version, and TrakSYS version.
Database Operations
Edit Connection
Repair Logins
Create / Upgrade Database
Backup / Restore Database
Transfer Export / Import
Audit Trigger Operations
(available when TrakSYS Audit features are licensed)
Create / Delete Audit Triggers

## Slide 8

Installation Manager: License

License Overview
Displays the current TrakSYS license and status. The TrakSYS license file must be imported into the database and activated for the software and components to be utilized. 
License Operations
Import License
Delete
Activate License Online
Activate License Manually
License Features
List the TrakSYS features from the current license. Allows the assignment of server name (Host) to license features which are required to be locked to a specific host machine.

## Slide 9

Installation Manager: Services

Services Overview
Lists the TrakSYS services that are currently installed on the local server. Includes the current server running status.
Web Operations
Install Logic
Install Historian
Install Data Management
Install Workflow
Install Maintenance
Web Operations
TrakSYS Services can be started, stopped and restarted from the Installation Manager. They can also be controlled from the standard Windows Services management interface. 

## Slide 10

Installation Manager: Webs

Web Application Overview
Displays the status of the TrakSYS web user interface application that is installed on Windows Internet Information Services (IIS). TrakSYS requires specific IIS features to be installed on the server in order to support its deployment and use.
Web Operations
Setup TS Web
Remove TS Web
Setup / Remove WEBTrak (legacy)

## Slide 11

Installation Manager: Other Features

Reporting Services
Allows management of TrakSYS reports hosted in SQL Reporting Services. Includes Reporting Services status and operations for installing and removing standard reports
Sites
Allows for the creation and management of TrakSYS Sites. This feature is only available when an appropriate multi-site license is present.
Diagnostics and Troubleshooting
Access to OPC and Mail connection statuses and TrakSYS log/trace entries. Includes operations to export application messages for convenient transport to support staff.

